      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft review for L'Aube Dorée bistro in Lyon:\n\nTucked away in the heart of Lyon, L'Aube Dorée is a gem of an intimate bistro that deftly balances upscale sophistication with a warm, inviting atmosphere. Upon entering, I was immediately enveloped in the soft glow of dim lighting, creating a sense of secluded luxury. The escargot, in particular, stood out – bursting with vibrant freshness, though perhaps a touch over-salted – a charming Italian classic. The main event, a slow-cooked duck breast, was nothing short of exceptional, its tender meat expertly paired with a sweet and tangy blackberry reduction that added a delightful depth of flavor. The lemon tart, too, shone, its sharp, zesty zing perfectly offset by a sublime, buttery crust. If service wasn't always as swift as the hosts had craved, the attentive team were more than eager to put right any oversight.",
